{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["A handful of its fine flour — the Sages interpreted in tractate Yoma: that he grasps with his three middle fingers." "Its memorial portion — the expression of regular 'mention,' to say: frankincense, because of the fragrance that rises. And so it is written: מזכיר לבונה. And likewise: והיתה ללחם לאזכרה. The types of meal offerings written here are spelled out in the tractate Meḥilt[a] — how many loaves each has, and how much frankincense, and how much oil in each one, and what is a מחבת and what is a מרחשת. Marcheshet — a deep vessel, and its contents bubble (רוחשין), but a machavat is not deep, and all of them come as matzah, as it says: צו את אהרן."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "I read מנחות as a reference to the halakhic midrash on Leviticus (Meḥilta de-Rabbi Shimon bar Yoḥai, also known as Meḥilta d'Achurei), consistent with the catalogue of grain-offering details that follows; the spelling מנחות may reflect a corrupted or abbreviated form of מחילתא."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:14.269002990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}